, 100000] (step 01); none returns event timestamps or restricts to [4765, 43165]. I therefore cannot verify (a) that the four single-occurrence edges fire in the required order, nor (b) that consecutive hops are within 600 time units. With ~16k events spread over 100k time units, a 4-hop chain of one-shot edges satisfying both ordering and the tight 600-unit relay bound is a priori unlikely, but that is an inference from base rates, not from temporal evidence \u2014 exactly what the task forbids as sufficient grounds.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_44f03991\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1330, 669, 199, 28, 361],\n  \"window\": [4765, 43165],\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"A static path 1330->669->199->28->361 exists (shortest possible; no 2- or 3-hop alternative), but it is mediated by hub node 28 (1204 events, 746 partners), so time-ignored reachability is uninformative. Each edge on the path occurs exactly once and the graph is near-simple (repeat ratio 0.042), leaving no redundancy to satisfy a 600-unit relay bound. Critically, all available tools aggregate over the full horizon [0,100000] and expose no timestamps or window filtering, so the ordering and <=600-unit gap conditions inside [4765,43165] cannot be checked. Evidence is insufficient to affirm or refute a genuine time-respecting cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 27478, "total_output_tokens": 6927, "total_tokens": 34405, "total_latency_ms": 92762, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}